    "task":  "No active task from the user — last request (a .bak-per-SQL-Server-database design question) was confirmed correct and closed. If resuming, first run `dotnet build MindAttic.Launcher.slnx -c Release` and `dotnet test MindAttic.Launcher.Tests -c Release` from the repo root to confirm the working tree (which now includes unreviewed parallel changes — see State) still compiles and passes before doing anything else.",
    "decisions":  "Settings menu API keys write through LlmCredentials to the shared MindAttic.Vault LlmCredentialStore (%APPDATA%\\MindAttic\\LLM\\providers.json) so other MindAttic apps can fall back to them. Claude is the one exception: ProviderCredentials.Apply never pushes ANTHROPIC_API_KEY when ClaudeAuthStatus.IsLoggedIntoClaudeAi() (checks ~/.claude/.credentials.json for a live claudeAiOauth session) is true, because the claude CLI itself warns that having both set makes auth unpredictable and claude.ai wins anyway. SQL Server backup stays one .bak per database (not one per server) - user explicitly confirmed this was correct, not a one-bak-per-instance design. SQLite backup support (SqliteBackupService, Project.SqliteDatabases) mirrors SqlBackupServices architecture: sqlite3 -readonly \u003cfile\u003e .dump written to a .sql file, with a pre-flight File.Exists check so sqlite3 is never invoked (and so never silently creates a db) at a missing path.",
    "state":  "Completed and tested by me this session: setup.ps1/setup.bat (first-time-setup wizard: workspace dir, desktop icon, example-repo roster seed); WindowsTerminalSchemes.CandidateSettingsPaths auto-detect + a Settings-menu row to set/clear the WT settings path; SettingsMenu API-key rows per provider (LlmCredentials.cs, new) wired into ProviderCredentials.Apply (added Claude-\u003eANTHROPIC_API_KEY, Codex-\u003eOPENAI_API_KEY mappings, both previously missing/inert); ClaudeAuthStatus.cs (new) gating Claude key injection behind claude.ai login state; SqliteBackupService.cs (new) + Project.SqliteDatabases + BackupMenu wired to collect/run/report SQLite dumps alongside SQL Server .bak and the file robocopy. docs/BIBLE.md + USER_STORIES.md (added MCO-US-D5) + README.md updated to match; `tools/codex.ps1 doctor` passes clean (done=23). Full test suite green at 214/214 as of my last check. IMPORTANT - since my last edit, files changed on disk outside my actions (not yet reviewed in depth by me): MainMenuCommand.cs gained an \"Orchestrator\" menu item that shells out to a separate MindAttic.Orchestrator.exe (C:\\Apps\\MindAttic.Orchestrator\\ or %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Programs\\MindAttic.Orchestrator\\, install-itself pattern); Program.cs, MindAttic.Launcher.csproj, MindAttic.Launcher.Tests.csproj, BackupService.cs and WindowsTerminalSchemes.cs are also modified; AppDataBackupService.cs is a new file (zips %APPDATA%\\MindAttic\\... settings into the dated backup folder - I only patched BackupMenu/MainMenuCommand call sites to compile against its new constructor param, did not write or review its internals); .claude/settings.json changed and .claude/hooks/quickload-on-do.ps1 + .claude/statusline.ps1 were deleted. A full `dotnet build` + `dotnet test` just before this save both passed clean, so the tree compiles as-is, but I have not read or reviewed most of these parallel changes.",
    "next":  "1. If picking this back up cold, re-run dotnet build + dotnet test first (see Task) since the tree has moved since my last full review. 2. Review the Orchestrator integration, AppDataBackupService.cs, and the other externally-changed files (Program.cs, the two .csproj files, BackupService.cs, WindowsTerminalSchemes.cs, .claude/settings.json) if asked to touch backup or menu code again, since I have not audited them. 3. No open task is waiting on me otherwise - nothing is half-done from my side.",
